#[section, $md:
    @../ (Developers) / Compiler-facing language reference

    # Compiler-facing language reference

    Compiler changes should start from the language contract. The unsuffixed
    references listed below own syntax, semantics, edge cases and deferred
    language surfaces.
]

#[section, $md:
    ## Canonical references

    Each public route groups the references for one language area.

    Foundations:

    - @../../docs/language-overview (Language basics)
    - @../../docs/bindings (Values and bindings)
    - @../../docs/numbers (Numbers)
    - @../../docs/casts (Casts)

    Functions and control flow:

    - @../../docs/functions (Functions)
    - @../../docs/branching (Branching)
    - @../../docs/loops (Loops)
    - @../../docs/errors (Errors, options and assertions)

    Data and compile-time construction:

    - @../../docs/structs (Structs)
    - @../../docs/choices (Choices)
    - @../../docs/collections (Collections and maps)
    - @../../docs/templates (Templates)
    - @../../docs/constants (Constants and compile-time behaviour)

    Names and static abstraction:

    - @../../docs/aliases (Aliases)
    - @../../docs/generics (Generics)
    - @../../docs/traits (Traits)

    UI state:

    - @../../docs/reactivity (Reactivity)

    Projects and imported content:

    - @../../docs/project-structure (Project structure)
    - @../../docs/packages (Packages and dependencies)
    - @../../docs/resources (Resources and file values)
    - @../../docs/moth-templates (Moth template files)
    - @../../docs/markdown (Plain Markdown)

    Each route combines a Basic teaching layer with detailed Advanced
    references. The unsuffixed Moth template files form the canonical language
    authority. Basic files and route introductions teach that contract without
    replacing it.
]

#[section, $md:
    ## Reference map

    `docs/src/developer-docs/language/overview.mtf` lists every canonical file and
    routes formal compiler, build and memory ownership.
]

#[section, $md:
    ## Related design

    - @../../docs/design-scope (Design scope, public authority): accepted mechanisms and intentionally excluded complexity
    - @../memory-management/access-and-aliasing (Access and aliasing): shared reads, explicit copies and exclusive access
    - @../compiler-design (Compiler design overview): stage ownership and cross-stage data flow
    - @../../docs/progress (Progress matrix): current implementation support and known gaps
]

#[section, $md:
    ## More documentation

    See @../../docs/ (All documentation) for tutorials, examples and feature-focused language pages.
]
